"The model to use for image generation: `dall-e-2`, `dall-e-3` or `gpt-image-1`. Defaults to `dall-e-2` unless a parameter specific to `gpt-image-1` is used.","Query the status and result of a video generation task.\n\nTask status:\n- `queued`: queued\n- `in_progress`: generating\n- `completed`: completed\n- `failed`: failed","Text description of the desired image. Maximum length is 32000 characters for `gpt-image-1`, 1000 for `dall-e-2` and 4000 for `dall-e-3`.","A unique identifier for your end user, which can help OpenAI monitor and detect abuse. [Learn more](https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/safety-best-practices/end-user-ids).","Open a WebSocket connection for realtime conversation.\n\n**Note**: this is a WebSocket endpoint; connect with the WebSocket protocol.\n\nExample connection URL: `wss://api.fathompeak.cn/v1/realtime?model=gpt-4o-realtime`","Video generation in the official Jimeng API format.\n\nSet the operation with the Action parameter:\n- `CVSync2AsyncSubmitTask`: submit a video generation task\n- `CVSync2AsyncGetResult`: get the task result\n\nAction and Version are required query parameters.","Get the list of currently available models.\n\nThe response format follows the request headers:\n- with `x-api-key` and `anthropic-version`: Anthropic format\n- with an `x-goog-api-key` header or a `key` query parameter: Gemini format\n- otherwise: OpenAI format","Allows setting transparency for the background of the generated image. Supported only by `gpt-image-1`. Must be one of `transparent`, `opaque` or `auto` (default). With `auto`, the model picks the best background for the image.\n\nIf `transparent`, the output format must support transparency, so set it to `png` (default) or `webp`.","Size of the generated images. For `gpt-image-1`, one of `1024x1024`, `1536x1024` (landscape), `1024x1536` (portrait) or `auto` (default); for `dall-e-2`, one of `256x256`, `512x512` or `1024x1024`; for `dall-e-3`, one of `1024x1024`, `1792x1024` or `1024x1792`.","OpenAI Responses API for creating model responses.\nSupports multi-turn conversations, tool calls, reasoning and more.\n\n### FathomPeak video\nWith the model `minimax-h3-fl2va`, you can submit text-to-video tasks through this endpoint (`input` maps to the prompt). It accepts the same fields as `/v1/videos` (`seconds` / `size` / `fps` / `num_inference_steps` / `flow_shift` / `seed` / `extra_params` and so on). When finished, it returns HTML that contains the video playback URL.",
"Proxies Gemini API requests.\nPath format: `/v1beta/models/{model_name}:{action}`\n\nFor example:\n- `/v1beta/models/gemini-2.5-pro:generateContent`\n- `/v1beta/models/gemini-2.5-pro:streamGenerateContent?alt=sse`\n\n\n---\n\n## Gemini media understanding\n\nImage, PDF, audio and video understanding requests for Gemini\n\n⚠️ Note: native Gemini requests can pass media as inlineData (base64) or fileData.fileUri (a publicly accessible URL; YouTube links are supported). Whether a file URI uploaded through the Gemini File API is accessible depends on the upstream service's permissions, so prefer publicly accessible URLs. When an OpenAI-format (chat/completions) request is converted to Gemini, media is downloaded and passed as inlineData (base64).\n\n---\n\n## Audio (native Gemini)\n\nGemini audio generation endpoint.\nWorks with models such as gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts",
"OpenAI-compatible video generation endpoint (`POST /v1/videos`).\n\n### Sora-compatible format\nReference: https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/videos/create\n\n### FathomPeak (Fathom / MiniMax-H3 FL2VA)\n- Model: `minimax-h3-fl2va`\n- Capability: text-to-video\n- Request: `application/json` or `multipart/form-data`\n- `seconds`: default 6, range 1–3600\n- `size`: `1024x576` | `1280x720` | `720x1280` | `576x1024` (default `1024x576`)\n- `fps`: fixed at `24`\n- `num_inference_steps`: 1–200, default 50\n- `flow_shift`: default 12\n- `seed`: default 42\n- `extra_params`: JSON, default `{\"task\":\"t2va\",\"duration\":<seconds>,\"audio_flow_shift\":3.0}`\n- Can also be called through `/v1/responses` (the Responses protocol); when finished it returns HTML with the video URL.",
